# T039 — Flow-matching final market-order wrapper

Owner: codex.  Status: in progress.  Never submit to Kaggle.

## Goal

Provide Claude a clean, self-contained template for a conditional flow-matching
advisor that may defer an already-emitted steep-product `SELL` from the final
`es7_wm` action.  It must be default-off and must not alter buys, hires, land,
or the promoted WHEAT market layer.

## Design contract

- Wrap the final `es7_wm` callable, i.e. after RACE, V92 queue, final-day
  planner and the appended WHEAT layer.
- Eligible products only: STRAWBERRY, MILK, WOOL, MELON, EGG, CARROT, TOMATO.
- The wrapper can only remove eligible `SELL` rows if the advisor says `hold`.
  It copies all other action fields and rows unchanged.
- No hold at `step >= 696`; no hold when total shed free space is below the
  explicit room floor.  The shipped advisor always returns `sell`, so it is
  action-identical to es7_wm even when the feature flag is enabled.
- Verify exact action identity on two deterministic official-engine worlds;
  record command, seeds and action-diff count here after the run.

