-# T039 — Flow-matching final market-order wrapper
+# T039 — Crop-mix substitution (redirected from market wrapper)
 
 Owner: codex.  Status: in progress.  Never submit to Kaggle.
 
-## Goal
+## Redirect (2026-09-26)
 
-Provide Claude a clean, self-contained template for a conditional flow-matching
-advisor that may defer an already-emitted steep-product `SELL` from the final
-`es7_wm` action.  It must be default-off and must not alter buys, hires, land,
-or the promoted WHEAT market layer.
+The steep-item SELL flow model has no usable signal (strawberry/milk/wool are
+within ±0.5pp of the hour baseline; only wheat/fertilizer/egg predict).  Drop
+the SELL-filter wrapper; no candidate or Kaggle action.
 
-## Design contract
+## New goal
+
+Build default-off `crop_mix` over final `es7_wm`.  It may replace an emitted
+tape `PLANT` with a crop selected toward a target mix, while retaining the
+worker/tile.  First fixed experiment: cap live STRAWBERRY at about 24 tiles
+(tops 21–29; es7 is 33) and use WHEAT instead for own feed.  Before allowing a
+replacement, prove seed accounting and the replacement crop's water/harvest
+path against the original tape; do not treat an ongoing STRAWBERRY/TOMATO tape
+as a finite WHEAT/CARROT path without a concrete compatible service schedule.
+
+## Gate
+
+1. Compile and exact default-off identity audit on two official-engine worlds.
+2. Enabled capability screen: two worlds, both seats, versus declared es7_wm
+control/opponents (≤6 workers).
+3. Only a survivor receives a fresh full-panel gate against `es7_wm`.
 
-- Wrap the final `es7_wm` callable, i.e. after RACE, V92 queue, final-day
-  planner and the appended WHEAT layer.
-- Eligible products only: STRAWBERRY, MILK, WOOL, MELON, EGG, CARROT, TOMATO.
-- The wrapper can only remove eligible `SELL` rows if the advisor says `hold`.
-  It copies all other action fields and rows unchanged.
-- No hold at `step >= 696`; no hold when total shed free space is below the
-  explicit room floor.  The shipped advisor always returns `sell`, so it is
-  action-identical to es7_wm even when the feature flag is enabled.
-- Verify exact action identity on two deterministic official-engine worlds;
-  record command, seeds and action-diff count here after the run.
+## Result
+
+Pending code/tape audit.

